  {
   "id": "FAM:SF19",
   "status_as_recorded": "supported",
   "finding": "Portability confirmatory test (T1): a mover's displacement signature is more similar across franchises than profile-matched destination decoys. Recorded median self_sim=+0.129 vs decoy_sim=+0.049; median Delta=+0.0557, perm p=0.0050; 173/294 positive (sign p=2.87e-3); destination-franchise CI [+0.0192,+0.0859]. Prereg record gave 296 movers, Delta=+0.0819."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF29",
   "what_failed": "Testing whether covering all three core roles in a lineup adds per-possession value net of role counts and talent.",
   "why": "Recorded as an adequately powered null (B_powered_null) with 72 team-seasons; the MDE80 was about 2.19 pts/100, so small role effects were not detectable at that sample size. The earlier estimate (+0.67 pts/100) and the later run (+0.42 pts/100) both fell well short of significance."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-032",
   "what_failed": "Using a travel x fit screen to predict post-move outcomes for movers.",
   "why": "Recorded as E_unclear. The correlation between delta and destination net rating was small (+0.077), fit-score correlations were negative, and thresholds were set in-sample. Its auto-recorded risks include LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD and OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Earlier work by this project on a related coverage question found that a 90 team-season design (72 with adequate possessions) could be run with the gating checks (within-team variation, separability from talent, talent control), but these checks were recorded only as feasibility gates.",
  "A confirmatory test on a related role-coverage hypothesis with 72 team-seasons returned a powered null, which indicates that role effects of the size plausibly at stake here were not reliably detectable at that sample size.",
  "A portability-style test (SF19) was recorded as supported with about 294 movers, showing that a mover-based displacement design can be run when the unit count is in the hundreds.",
  "A related outcome-screen (SF-PAP-032) with 198 movers was recorded as inconclusive, with outcome-derived labels and in-sample thresholds flagged as risks."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "None of the retrieved records tests cut-heavy versus drive-heavy shaper roles or their portability. All records concern coverage or travel/fit or displacement signatures, so the retrieved evidence is adjacent, not direct.",
  "Nothing retrieved shows that n=24 units suffices. The closest powered analogue (72 team-seasons) returned a null with a large MDE, which points the other way.",
  "No retrieved record establishes how cut-heavy and drive-heavy shapers should be classified from play-type data, or whether that classification is stable across seasons and playoffs.",
